Types
*****

.[perex]
The `types` section decides on types in declarations: whether parameters, properties, return values and class constants must declare a type, how a nullable type is written and where `null` goes in it, and in what order the types of a union go.

The keys under `declaration` add the native type of a parameter, a property, a return value, a constant and a closure where the doc comment already states it. The decision `phpdoc.annotation.nativeTypeOnly` then removes an annotation that only repeats the native type, so the example sets it as well. A parameter that has neither a type nor an annotation is only reported: nobody can invent the type for you. The parameter `traversableClasses` says which classes to treat like an array whose items the annotation describes. Types in doc comments belong to the [phpdoc |phpdoc] section. The reserved key `typeAnalysis` decides where DressCode gets the types of expressions from, and the [Types from PHPStan |/types] page explains it.

```neon
types:
	declaration:
		parameter: required
		return: required
	nullable: '?int'
phpdoc:
	annotation:
		nativeTypeOnly: forbidden
```

```php .[before]
/**  // Useless `@param` annotation for the parameter `$count`, because the native type says the same.
 * @param int $count
 */
function repeat(string $text, $count, ?string $glue = null): string  // The parameter `$count` must have the native type `int` from its `@param` annotation.
{
	return implode($glue ?? '', array_fill(0, $count, $text));
}
```

```php .[after]
function repeat(string $text, int $count, ?string $glue = null): string
{
	return implode($glue ?? '', array_fill(0, $count, $text));
}
```


types.traversableClasses
========================

Classes treated like `array` and `iterable`, whose annotation says what their items are.

- a list of names

Default `[Traversable]` · standards: perCs `[Traversable]`, psr12 `[Traversable]`, nette `[Traversable]`, symfony `[Traversable]`, laravel `[Traversable]` .[decision-facts]


types.declaration.parameter
===========================

A parameter of a function or a method declares its type, taken from `@param` where it has one and nullable where it defaults to null; one with neither, and one whose annotation PHP cannot write, is reported.

Not a parameter of a closure, whose types belong to the call it is passed to.

- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `phpdoc_to_param_type`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.ParameterTypeHint` .[decision-facts]


types.declaration.property
==========================

A property declares its type, a promoted one included, taken from `@var`, or the `@param` of a promoted one, where it has one and nullable where it defaults to null, `= null` written where an untyped one had no default.

- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `phpdoc_to_property_type`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.PropertyTypeHint` .[decision-facts]


types.declaration.return
========================

A function or a method declares its return type, taken from `@return`, `void` where it returns no value and `never` where the annotation says so.

- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `phpdoc_to_return_type`, `void_return`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.ReturnTypeHint` .[decision-facts]


types.declaration.anonymousFunction
===================================

A closure declares its return type `void` where it returns no value.

Not an arrow function, whose value is its expression.

- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `void_return`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.ReturnTypeHint` .[decision-facts]


types.declaration.constant
==========================

A class constant declares the type of its value.

- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · PHP 8.3 · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]


types.nullable
==============

How a native type of one type and `null` is written.

- `'?int'`: a single type with `null` written with `?`
- `'int|null'`: a union with `null`, which `types.nullPosition` places
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `'?int'`, psr12 `keep`, nette `'?int'`, symfony `'?int'`, laravel `'?int'` · covers `nullable_type_declaration` .[decision-facts]


types.nullPosition
==================

Where `null` stands in a native union type.

- `last`: `int|string|null`
- `first`: `null|int|string`
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `last`, psr12 `keep`, nette `last`, symfony `last`, laravel `keep` · covers `ordered_types` .[decision-facts]


types.unionOrder
================

The order of the types of a native union.

- `alphabetical`: the types beside `null` sorted by name, case-insensitively, an intersection by its first name
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `ordered_types` .[decision-facts]
